WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:00.680
Flowers and Labors

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:07.640
Springtime
Traffic
Safety
Campaign

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.600
Labor Pilot Safety
Seminar

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.690
You have to exercise caution
in rain and bad weather...

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.190
where poor footing compounds
decrease visibility.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:23.160
Even in normal weather,
fog and gusts of wind can affect...

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.250
uh, affect the situation.
Uh...

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.630
The wind, uh, and fog...

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.590
Who's that guy?
Japanese Mafia?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.260
Shh! He'll hear you!

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:43.180
Hey, button it up.
I'm trying to listen here.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.180
Go ahead, teacher.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:49.140
Yes, uh, thank you.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.770
To continue...

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.030
We will now demonstrate
proper transport of materials.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.900
The horizontal carry.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.030
The vertical carry.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:05.160
Above the head.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:11.460
When carrying over the shoulder,
be extra careful during turns.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.750
Don't rely on your monitor;
use your eyes as well.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.710
That concludes
today's safety training.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:19.920
Thank you very much.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.550
Hey, girlie.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.010
Girlie?

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:30.020
Nice little machine you got there.
How's it work?

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.980
Is it one of those
voice activated jobs?

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.440
No, there's a pilot on board.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:43.320
Well look at that!
The pilot's a dame!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.700
Not in a million years
did I expect to see that.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:48.410
Well, see you!

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.380
They aren't ready
for you to board yet.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.800
Roger.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.090
No one looks like that.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:05.430
They were <i>yakuza</i>
straight out of a gangster movie.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.720
And why would movie gangsters
attend a safety course?

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.640
Better yet,
why would they need Labors?

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.140
You can't stereotype people.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.940
Hi, toots!

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.320
Hello.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.980
See!

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.400
What's on the ticket today?

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.410
We're moving the Labor out.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.790
Right. Last time was just a
dry run, but this is the real McCoy.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.080
Oh, I forgot to introduce myself.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:36.460
My card.
The pleasure's all mine.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.420
"Hanafuji Group, Leader
Naoya Fujioka."

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:43.050
Give me a ring if you ever
find yourself in trouble.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.430
Oh, but you're the cops!

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.550
I guess we're in what
you'd call the same business.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.060
Well, you've probably
got things to do.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.980
I'll watch from over there.
Good luck!

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.650
This looks like trouble.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:04:59.940
I told you so!

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:03.400
Well, I can only think
of one thing...

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.530
They want to use
labors as weapons.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:08.620
You let criminals
into your presentation?

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:11.740
I'd have given them
six inches of my boot!

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.540
Labors <i>are</i> allowed
to carry weapons.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:19.250
And anyone is legally
entitled to own a Labor.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.880
A recipe for disaster.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.840
He seemed like
such a nice old guy.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.800
Bye!

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.760
Night!

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:34.100
What are you up to tomorrow?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.560
I have to pack for my trip home.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:40.860
Get back!

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.320
Hey, it's the dames!

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.620
Welcome home.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.370
Is he here?

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:58.500
No, he postponed things
until tomorrow.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.380
I smell a trap.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:03.380
Oh, well.
Show them the layout.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.800
I'll join you soon.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:13.560
This way.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:17.600
This is it.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.290
Sweet setup, isn't it?

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:46.260
The 98-AV Ingram was a bit
out of my price range.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.510
You cops can afford them
of course.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:52.680
I should be getting in
a German model tomorrow.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:55.220
I'm thinking of getting
an Italian job too.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.980
What will you do
with all these Labors?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.140
It's my collection.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.770
- Collection?!
- Yup.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.440
I used to collect Japanese
swords and classic cars.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.190
Labors are lots
classier than that junk!

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:13.660
It'll take a while to collect them all,
but it's worth it.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:18.120
You use them for digging
and moving cargo, don't you?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.120
That's what they're made for!

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:24.290
Hey, the manuals are
all about three feet thick!

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:27.340
They're impossible to read,
so nobody here can drive the Labors!

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.840
But the manuals make
great book ends!

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.340
- It's not funny!
- No, sir!

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:39.810
Wow! Noa,
what did you DO for this?

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:43.650
I just told him how to
activate the default settings.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.820
- YOU did?
- Kanuka explained most of it.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.030
Is it all right to accept this gift?

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.320
Wait!

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:55.280
They might be trying to
pry secret information out of us!

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.080
Don't worry.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.750
If they can't even master
the default settings...

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:04.750
they wouldn't know what to do
with advanced information from us.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.250
How splendid!

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.170
Captain!
We as policemen...

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.880
It'll go bad
if we don't eat it soon.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:14.680
But, sir, this is...

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:17.300
- He's right; let's dig in.
- Hey!

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:19.810
- Sounds good!
- Hey, you guys!

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.230
Keep talking;
it leaves more for us.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:26.150
The entire team is
responsible for proper conduct!

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.320
Dibs on the cucumber rolls!

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:29.610
Think we care?!

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.900
Hello, Second Section here.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.910
One moment, please.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.580
Izumi speaking.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:46.290
We wanted to thank you
for your help.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.830
Oh, you're from
the Hanafuji Group.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:54.300
Oh, it's nothing; simply an
expression of gratitude.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.090
The boss has been practicing
since you left.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:09:00.260
He'd like to
show you his progress.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:04.230
Look what I can do!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.690
We don't want to bother you.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:14.150
But we'd appreciate it
if you could give us a few pointers.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.660
Let's go!
Bring the car around!

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.100
Does he think
this is a rice field?

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.890
How was that?
Anything I should work on?

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:49.020
You need to learn to move
both of your feet at once.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:52.360
If you can't do that,
you'll trip.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.320
I see!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.530
But you show good aptitude;
you'll improve with practice.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:58.990
Really?

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:01.660
Boss.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.910
What, is it that time already?

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:08.750
Sorry I've got a meeting
and I have to be off.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.080
Maybe I could
drop in on you later.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:14.550
Certainly, as long as
we're not busy.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.430
Was it wise to tell him that?

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:23.430
He <i>did</i> give us a gift;
I couldn't help myself.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:28.940
This concludes our meeting.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:32.190
I'd like to thank the leaders
of Hanafuji and Daina for coming.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.900
- Good evening!
- Welcome!

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.660
So, are you still working
on your collection?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:45.120
Yeah, I finally picked up
that beauty of a sword.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.790
The Mitsumasa blade?

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:52.380
You had your eye
on the sword too, didn't you?

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:56.300
Well, the race goes to the swift.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.840
I hope you're not
too disappointed.

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.970
Not at all;
not a jealous bone in me.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:04.100
I couldn't be happier.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.770
Labors, my old friend.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:11.020
That's where the action is,
not in old swords and relics!

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.850
That's what you
should be collecting!

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:19.360
It sounds like
you already have quite a few.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.030
My collection is
the biggest in Japan.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:27.910
Perhaps in the top 5
in the whole world.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:34.040
In that case, you'll have to
show me sometime.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.590
Of course, any time.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:58.280
Graubear
(customized)

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:17.460
And my latest is the crown jewel;
I'll show you it.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:23.010
A German multi-use Labor:
The Graubear.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:27.970
I'm the first man to purchase
one for personal use.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:32.890
Cost me a pretty penny,
but it was worth it.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:36.940
Yeah, that's pretty good.
I have to admit, I'm impressed.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:40.650
Word on the street is that
you just bought a Labor too.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:45.990
Yeah, but it's not my thing
to collect so many like you do.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.320
I just own one.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:51.410
Oh yeah?
You'll have to show it to me.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.220
Here it is.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:06.550
It may not be much to look at.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.270
That's...!

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.100
It's a Graubear,
heavily customized.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.270
It's five times the cost
of the regular model.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.860
But it's the only one
of its kind in the world.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:28.200
Even a hick can buy labors
with enough cash.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:33.700
The most important thing is
to spend the time to perfect it.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.380
Boss, it's time for your practice.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.880
Yeah, I'm coming.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:54.850
I never should have showed him.
Daina outdid me again!

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:57.600
And I had finally learned
how to skip in it too!

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:01.820
You can't give up, boss.
After all you're still a better pilot.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:06.700
You're right!
Goto said I had aptitude!

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:09.200
There's still a way
I can outdo Daina!

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:13.790
Hello?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:18.750
Oh, nice to hear from you.
Yes, we're all fine.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:23.630
One moment, please.
Izumi, it's Fujioka.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:25.210
Hello?

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.050
Hey, long time, no talk.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:31.970
I have a little favor to ask you.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.640
What is it?
Did you get a system error?

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:36.470
Nope, nothing like that.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:38.690
I want to work for
Special Vehicles, Second Section.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.400
I won't use money on you.
None of that mafia things.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:47.150
I'm thinking I ought to be helping out
in my local neighborhood.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.860
That's certainly
a nice thought, but...

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:54.620
All 1,500 members of the Hanafuji
Group would be at your disposal.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.910
That's not really the point...

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:01.000
305 in sector 4!
Division 2: Mobilize.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.960
Sorry, I'll have to call you back.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:16.100
What took ya so long?!
I've been waiting 30 minutes!

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:17.930
Why are you here?

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:19.560
Like they say, "it takes a thief."

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:22.900
I just happened to be listening
to my police scanner.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:27.820
Seems there was trouble between
these two Labors, but I took care of it.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.820
From now on, you won't have
to handle this sort of trouble.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.620
Just leave it to me!

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.080
Oh, man!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:49.340
In honor of the timely assistance
of Mr. Naoya Fujioka.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:56.180
Isn't this like putting out
a fire with gasoline?

00:15:56.810 --> 00:16:02.190
The chief will be
on guard from now on.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.690
But we're the ones
who encouraged Fujioka.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:10.490
But what'll we do if he decides
he likes this and keeps it up?

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:12.450
Yes, what will we do?

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:18.450
My! It says
"Official Commendation!"

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.160
Oh, it's nothing.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.000
You see, Daina...

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:30.840
a Labor isn't worth squat
if you can't use it.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.010
It could cost a fortune...

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:37.850
but if you don't know how to use it,
it's a joke!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.850
Mr. Fujioka, you're so incredible!

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.730
I think I'm falling in love!

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:46.980
If I'm ever in danger,
will you save me?

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:51.320
Of course I will, darling!
I'll be there for ya!

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.820
I need some wire taps!
Get on it!

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:57.990
Two can play at this game!

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:03.250
Sector 1: 501 in progress
in Chiyoda.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.910
Criminal is fleeing in a stolen Labor.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.670
Mobilize unit 1 in
Second Section, Division 2.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.500
Boss, it's in Chiyoda!

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.880
Which one is unit 1?

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.260
I'm pretty sure it's Izumi's.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:15.340
Perfect!

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:18.050
Don't worry, Izumi,
Fujioka is on his way!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:23.770
He won't outdo me!
Hurry!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:33.820
Freeze!

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:38.950
Hold it!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.790
The criminal is
fleeing toward Shibuya.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:47.920
What's this?

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:51.500
The stolen Labor is now fighting
two other Labors in Yotsuya!

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.760
The pilots of the two new
Labors are unknown.

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:55.840
Investigating!

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:59.550
You don't suppose that would be...

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.100
Don't say any more, Hiromi!

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:06.310
Out of my way!
This is your last warning!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:10.060
I saw him first!
I wish you'd butt out!

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:14.780
I'm getting pretty sick of
looking at your ugly mug!

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.650
You need a reality check.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:22.240
I have speed and intuitive talent
on my side; you have squat.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.410
That's it!
You're going down!

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.680
Don't move an inch, bozo!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:42.760
I'll deal with you later!
Stay put, loser!

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:45.890
Stop this!

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:48.140
Izumi!

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.900
Just what do you think
you're doing here?

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.900
Your actions prove that
you're unfit for this line of duty!

00:18:56.230 --> 00:19:00.160
You aren't heroes;
you're the criminals!

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:04.870
You're in no position
to judge other people!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:11.920
If you continue this further
you'll have to answer to <i>me</i>!

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:19.920
I'm glad they calmed down.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.550
Maybe I was too harsh.

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:24.550
Who's calling at this hour?

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:26.760
Second Section.

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:30.520
Izumi... thank goodness!
We've got trouble!

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.310
Boss, don't do it!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:34.480
Let go!
There IS honor among thieves!

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:35.320
It's the boss!

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.340
Asuma! Asuma!

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.630
Bring Alphonse! It's a turf war!

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:13.100
Fear me, Fujioka!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:18.190
I don't even fear a raging fire.
You're a dead man.

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:19.860
I seriously doubt it!

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:27.410
Where's Fujioka?

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.120
- He's in a Labor fighting Daina.
- What?!

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:38.040
You've gotta get out of here!

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:40.630
Asuma, hurry!

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:46.180
Noa! What's going on?

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.640
Kanuka?

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:55.020
Let's put a halt to foolishness.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.570
Knock it off!

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:06.660
This time he's gone too far!
I'm going to cut him up!

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.370
Over my dead body!

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.540
Butt out!

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:17.250
- I got her!
- Why, you!

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:22.170
Why can't you settle down...

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:26.550
and talk this out
between yourselves?!

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:57.790
- Miss!
- No excuses!

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:12.720
Labor operating disks?

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:18.190
All of mine and Daina's.
Do what you want with them.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:20.020
ALL the Labors?

00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:24.860
I'll let you people operate Labors;
they're too dangerous.

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:29.030
A regular life of crime
is much safer.

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:34.490
I've had my fill of danger
for a while.

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:45.380
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:49.090
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:55.350
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:04.860
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:07.780
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:12.370
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:17.040
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:19.870
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:24.040
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:30.550
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:35.810
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:38.350
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:41.560
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:45.650
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:51.820
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:53.990 --> 00:23:57.870
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:04.500
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:09.210
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:09.210
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:17.470
Kanuka finished six months training,
and she's turning in her uniform.

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:19.680
We planned a farewell
surprise party for Kanuka...

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:22.230
so we hid out in her apartment.

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:25.060
That's where we found
Kanuka's training report.

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:27.980
She gave perfect marks to
everyone including Captain Goto.

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:29.320
It can't hurt to look
if she doesn't find out.

00:24:29.320 --> 00:24:32.240
That's not right!
Don't you guys ever look at mine!

00:24:32.570 --> 00:24:36.320
Next time, "Kanuka's Report."
Target, locked on!

00:24:35.490 --> 00:24:40.700
Next episode

00:24:35.490 --> 00:24:40.700
Kanuka’s Report
